# Cloudflare Pages: first match wins — specific rules first.

# Scorer-exam upload: the page was announced with the umlaut spelling, but every slug on
# this site is ASCII, so /pruefung is canonical and the umlaut 301s onto it. Both the
# percent-encoded and the raw form are listed — browsers send the encoded one, but link
# checkers, QR readers and pasted-from-chat URLs do turn up raw.
/weiteres/schreiberkurse/pr%C3%BCfung   /weiteres/schreiberkurse/pruefung   301
/weiteres/schreiberkurse/prüfung        /weiteres/schreiberkurse/pruefung   301

# The legacy locale URLs of the single-URL migration (/de, /en, /de/* and /en/*,
# including the translated-slug and retired-page ones) are NOT redirected here any
# more: they live in functions/_middleware.js (2026-09-28). As `/de/*  /:splat  301`
# they were an open redirect — `/de//evil.example` became `Location: //evil.example`
# — and a splat cannot be normalised in this file. Do not add a /de or /en rule
# here: Cloudflare skips `_redirects` for requests a Function serves, and
# public/_routes.json sends every /de and /en request to the Function, so such a
# rule would silently never fire.
